Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Monknot landing page.

## What was implemented:

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics following the latest official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart).

## Changes made:

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 2.0.1)
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
Added Vercel Analytics script tags to all three HTML pages:
- **index.html**: Added analytics scripts before closing `</body>` tag
- **support.html**: Added analytics scripts before closing `</body>` tag  
- **privacy.html**: Added analytics scripts before closing `</body>` tag

The integration follows the vanilla/static site pattern from the official docs:
```html
<script>
  window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
```

### 3. Build Script Updates
- **scripts/check.mjs**: Updated the local file validation logic to exclude Vercel-specific paths (/_vercel/*) from file existence checks, as these are provided by Vercel's platform at runtime.

### 4. Git Configuration
- **.gitignore**: Added `node_modules/` to ensure the dependency directory is not tracked in version control (standard practice for Node.js projects).

## Framework Detection:

This project is a vanilla JavaScript static website (not a framework like Next.js or React). The appropriate installation method for vanilla sites was used based on the official documentation.

## Verification:

✅ Build successful (`npm run build`)
✅ All tests pass (`npm run check`)
✅ Analytics scripts correctly included in all built HTML files in the `dist` folder
✅ No linting errors introduced
✅ Lock files properly updated

## Notes:

- The `/_vercel/insights/script.js` path is a special Vercel-provided resource that only exists in production on Vercel's platform
- Analytics will start collecting data once the site is deployed to Vercel
- To view analytics data, the project owner needs to enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
- The implementation preserves all existing code structure and only adds the minimal necessary changes
